<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
  <meta name="color-scheme" content="dark light">
  <title>Private QR Code Generator for Links, Text & Wi-Fi | Christa Vakoli</title>
  <meta name="description" content="Create colored QR codes for URLs, text and Wi-Fi credentials. Download PNG or vector SVG directly from your browser.">
  <meta property="og:type" content="website">
  <meta property="og:url" content="https://christavakoli.com/tools/qr-generator.html">
  <meta property="og:title" content="Private QR Code Generator">
  <meta property="og:description" content="Generate custom PNG and SVG QR codes locally.">
  <link rel="canonical" href="https://christavakoli.com/tools/qr-generator.html">
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="../css/tools.css">
  <script type="application/ld+json">
    {
      "@context": "https://schema.org",
      "@type": "WebApplication",
      "name": "Private QR Code Generator",
      "url": "https://christavakoli.com/tools/qr-generator.html",
      "applicationCategory": "UtilitiesApplication",
      "operatingSystem": "Any modern browser",
      "description": "Create QR codes for URLs, text and Wi-Fi with PNG and SVG downloads."
    }
  </script>
  <script src="https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/qrcodejs/1.0.0/qrcode.min.js" defer></script>
  <script src="../js/shared.js" defer></script>
  <script src="../js/qr-tools.js" defer></script>
</head>
<body class="utility-site" data-home="./">
  <div id="tools-header"></div>

  <main class="wrap main-content">
    <h1>QR code generator</h1>
    <p class="page-intro">Make custom QR codes for links, plain text and Wi-Fi.</p>

    <!-- AD_SLOT_TOP: Paste an optional ad snippet inside this empty container. -->
    <div class="ad-slot" aria-label="Advertisement"></div>

    <div id="error-banner" class="error-banner" role="alert" hidden></div>

    <div class="tool-layout">
      <div class="stack">
        <section class="panel" aria-labelledby="generator-heading">
          <h2 id="generator-heading">Create a QR code</h2>

          <label for="qr-kind">QR content</label>
          <select id="qr-kind">
            <option value="url">Website URL</option>
            <option value="text">Plain text</option>
            <option value="wifi">Wi-Fi credentials</option>
          </select>

          <div id="url-controls">
            <label for="qr-url">Website URL</label>
            <input id="qr-url" type="url"
                   placeholder="https://example.com"
                   autocomplete="url">
          </div>

          <div id="text-controls" hidden>
            <label for="qr-text">Plain text</label>
            <textarea id="qr-text"
                      placeholder="Type the text to encode"></textarea>
          </div>

          <div id="wifi-controls" hidden>
            <label for="wifi-ssid">Network name (SSID)</label>
            <input id="wifi-ssid" type="text"
                   autocomplete="off">

            <label for="wifi-security">Security</label>
            <select id="wifi-security">
              <option value="WPA">WPA / WPA2 / WPA3 Personal</option>
              <option value="WEP">WEP</option>
              <option value="nopass">Open network</option>
            </select>

            <div id="wifi-password-controls">
              <label for="wifi-password">Wi-Fi password</label>
              <input id="wifi-password" type="text"
                     autocomplete="off">
            </div>

            <label>
              <input id="wifi-hidden" type="checkbox">
              Hidden network
            </label>
          </div>

          <div class="cols-2">
            <div>
              <label for="qr-foreground">Foreground</label>
              <input id="qr-foreground" type="color" value="#111827">
            </div>

            <div>
              <label for="qr-background">Background</label>
              <input id="qr-background" type="color" value="#ffffff">
            </div>
          </div>

          <p class="hint">
            Use contrasting colors for reliable scanning. Wi-Fi passwords
            are encoded in the QR code itself; share the image only with
            people you want to give access to.
          </p>

          <div class="actions">
            <button id="generate-qr" type="button" class="btn primary">
              Generate QR code
            </button>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section class="panel" aria-labelledby="preview-heading">
          <h2 id="preview-heading">Preview and download</h2>

          <div id="qr-preview" class="qr-preview"
               aria-label="Generated QR code preview">
            <p class="hint">Your QR code will appear here.</p>
          </div>

          <div class="actions">
            <button id="download-qr-png" type="button" class="btn"
                    disabled>Download PNG</button>
            <button id="download-qr-svg" type="button" class="btn"
                    disabled>Download SVG</button>
          </div>
        </section>

        <p class="privacy-notice">
          Privacy: QR content is processed locally on your device and is never uploaded.
          Anyone who receives a generated QR image can read its encoded content.
        </p>
      </div>

      <aside>
        <!-- AD_SLOT_SIDEBAR: Paste an optional ad snippet inside this empty container. -->
        <div class="ad-slot" aria-label="Advertisement"></div>
      </aside>
    </div>

    <section class="faq" aria-labelledby="faq-heading">
      <h2 id="faq-heading">How it works & FAQ</h2>

      <div class="panel">
        <h3>How do I create a Wi-Fi QR code?</h3>
        <p>Select Wi-Fi, enter the network name and security details, then generate the code. Scan it with a compatible device to join the network.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="panel">
        <h3>What is the difference between PNG and SVG?</h3>
        <p>PNG is a pixel image. SVG is vector artwork and can be enlarged without becoming blurry.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="panel">
        <h3>Is it safe to share a Wi-Fi QR code?</h3>
        <p>Only share it with people you trust. A Wi-Fi QR code contains the network details, including its password when you enter one.</p>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>

  <div id="tools-footer"></div>
</body>
</html>
